### Component 4: License Service Rewrite

#### [MODIFY] [device_license.dart](file:///c:/Users/Moazzam%20Samoo/Desktop/Tahir%20Showroom/lib/app/core/license/device_license.dart)

Replace the hardcoded check with Firebase + permanent cache:

```dart
import 'dart:io';
import 'package:cloud_firestore/cloud_firestore.dart';
import 'package:shared_preferences/shared_preferences.dart';

/// Fetches the unique Motherboard UUID from the current Windows device
/// using PowerShell. This UUID is permanent and unrelated to network adapters.
///
/// Returns the UUID string, or 'UNKNOWN_DEVICE_ID' on failure.
Future<String> getDeviceUuid() async {
  if (!Platform.isWindows) {
    return 'UNSUPPORTED_PLATFORM';
  }

  try {
    final result = await Process.run(
      'powershell',
      ['-NoProfile', '-Command', '(Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_ComputerSystemProduct).UUID'],
      runInShell: true,
    );

    if (result.exitCode != 0) return 'UNKNOWN_DEVICE_ID';

    final output = (result.stdout as String).trim();
    if (output.isEmpty) return 'UNKNOWN_DEVICE_ID';

    return output.toUpperCase();
  } catch (_) {
    return 'UNKNOWN_DEVICE_ID';
  }
}

/// Device license gatekeeper — checks Firebase Firestore for first-time
/// registration, then caches authorization permanently.
///
/// Strategy:
///   - First launch: MUST have internet → checks Firebase → caches forever
///   - Subsequent launches: uses cache (no internet needed)
///   - If internet is available: silently re-checks Firebase (for revocation)
///   - Cache persists until app is uninstalled
class DeviceLicense {
  DeviceLicense._();

  static const _keyAuthorized = 'device_license_authorized';

  static Future<({bool authorized, String deviceId})> isDeviceAuthorized() async {
    final deviceId = await getDeviceUuid();
    final prefs = await SharedPreferences.getInstance();
    final cachedAuth = prefs.getBool(_keyAuthorized);

    // ── CASE 1: Already cached (previously registered) ──
    if (cachedAuth != null) {
      // If cached as authorized, try a quick background re-check for revocation
      if (cachedAuth) {
        _backgroundRevocationCheck(deviceId, prefs);
      }
      return (authorized: cachedAuth, deviceId: deviceId);
    }

    // ── CASE 2: First time (no cache) — must check Firebase ──
    try {
      final doc = await FirebaseFirestore.instance
          .collection('allowed_devices')
          .doc(deviceId)
          .get()
          .timeout(const Duration(seconds: 10));

      final authorized = doc.exists && (doc.data()?['active'] == true);

      // Cache the result permanently
      await prefs.setBool(_keyAuthorized, authorized);

      return (authorized: authorized, deviceId: deviceId);
    } catch (_) {
      // No internet on first launch → deny (must register online first)
      return (authorized: false, deviceId: deviceId);
    }
  }

  /// Silent background check — does NOT block app launch.
  /// If Firebase says revoked, updates the cache so NEXT launch will deny.
  static void _backgroundRevocationCheck(String deviceId, SharedPreferences prefs) {
    // Fire-and-forget — runs in background, doesn't block the app
    FirebaseFirestore.instance
        .collection('allowed_devices')
        .doc(deviceId)
        .get()
        .timeout(const Duration(seconds: 3))
        .then((doc) {
      final stillActive = doc.exists && (doc.data()?['active'] == true);
      if (!stillActive) {
        // Revoked! Update cache — next app launch will deny access
        prefs.setBool(_keyAuthorized, false);
      }
    }).catchError((_) {
      // No internet or timeout — do nothing, keep cached authorization
    });
  }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**
- **First launch** requires internet — 10-second timeout for initial registration
- **Subsequent launches** — app opens instantly from cache, no internet needed ever
- **Background revocation** — 3-second silent check, fire-and-forget. If revoked, updates cache so **next** app launch denies access. Current session is not interrupted.
- **Cache is permanent** — only cleared by uninstalling the app (SharedPreferences is stored in AppData)

